     "quote": "The Vision Transformer (ViT), used for image encoding, is initialized with CLIP ViT-H/14 model~\\citep{ilharco_gabriel_2021_5143773}. A Projection Module, designed to align image features with text feature spcae, consists of a two-layer Multilayer Perceptron (MLP) with layer normalizations.",
     "where": "Sec. Vision-Language"
    },
    {
     "mechanism": "Yi-9B depth upscaling: Yi-6B's 32 layers expanded to 48 by duplicating middle layers 12-28, then continued pretraining (separate variant)",
     "quote": "our goal is to upscale our Yi-6B base model, which has 32 layers, to a 9B model named the Yi-9B base model, featuring 48 layers, by duplicating the original 16 middle layers 12-28.",
     "where": "Sec. Depth Upscaling"
    }
   ],
   "notes": "I describe the base Yi-6B and Yi-34B pretrained models, with Yi-6B as the primary config; block_ops attribute values are for Yi-6B. The paper says the code is based on LLaMA's implementation. On that basis I marked RMSNorm, pre-norm placement and the residual connections as inherited from LLaMA; the paper never names them itself. Values left not_stated: head_dim, d_ff, norm eps, rope pairing and rope theta, biases, and weight tying. For d_ff the paper only gives the ratio 8/3h, not a number. For rope theta it says the base frequency is adjusted (RoPE ABF) but gives no value. The 200K-context, chat, VL and 9B models are extensions of this base model and are not described here."
  },
